# Datasets are never committed. They are cited in Section 3.2 of the report
# instead, and the submission ZIP must not contain them. This is not only
# policy: data/HRIPCB.zip alone is 1.9 GB, and GitHub rejects any single file
# over 100 MB, so committing it would fail the push outright.
data/

# Generated artefacts are ignored by default...
*.csv
*.png

# ...with deliberate exceptions. Figures used in the report live under docs/,
# and everything under outputs/ is committed so the team can read the metrics
# and use the figures without rerunning every benchmark first.
!docs/**/*.png
!outputs/**/*.csv
!outputs/**/*.png

# Run logs are noise, not results.
outputs/*.txt
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
